\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Two independent exact enumerations give 226 primitive symbolic cycles through period 20. The interval-factor quotient changes only one primitive boundary pair: it adds the fixed point \(d\) at period one and removes the symbolic orbit \(1\leftrightarrow 2\) at period two. All higher primitive-count differences vanish. Candidate instability lengths occupy the rank-one lattice \(\{k\qopname  \relax o{log}2:k\geq 1\}\), whose rational-prime intersection is only \(\qopname  \relax o{log}2\).}}{10}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:orbit-lattice}{{2}{10}{Two independent exact enumerations give 226 primitive symbolic cycles through period 20. The interval-factor quotient changes only one primitive boundary pair: it adds the fixed point \(d\) at period one and removes the symbolic orbit \(1\leftrightarrow 2\) at period two. All higher primitive-count differences vanish. Candidate instability lengths occupy the rank-one lattice \(\{k\log 2:k\geq 1\}\), whose rational-prime intersection is only \(\log 2\)}{figure.2}{}}
